DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260115
SUMMARY:⚪ St Hilary\, Bishop\, Confessor & Doctor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Epiphany\nMass: Mass of the fe
 ast (Proper of Saints\, 14 Jan\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Felix\, Pr
 iest & Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Common\nBishop of Poiti
 ers in Gaul (c. 310–367)\, exiled to Phrygia in 356 for refusing to cond
 emn Athanasius. His De Trinitate made him the chief Latin opponent of Aria
 nism\; declared a Doctor in 1851.\nSt Hilary · patron of Poitiers\, child
 ren slow to learn\, against snakebites\nSt. Hilary Novena: https://www.pra
 ymorenovenas.com/st-hilary-novena\nPriest of Nola near Naples\, imprisoned
  and tortured under Decius around 250\, who survived and died in peace abo
 ut 260. Paulinus of Nola wrote yearly poems at his tomb in the late 4th ce
 ntury.\nSt Felix · patron of Nola\, against perjury\, eye diseases\nSt. F
 elix Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-felix-novena\nMass propers
  (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.
 pl?date1=01-14-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&la
 ng2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficiu
 m.pl?date1=01-14-2026&command=prayLaudes&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960
 &lang2=English\nVespers: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pof
 ficium.pl?date1=01-14-2026&command=prayVesperae&version=Rubrics%201960%20-
 %201960&lang2=English\nCompline: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/h
 oras/Pofficium.pl?date1=01-14-2026&command=prayCompletorium&version=Rubric
 s%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CATEGORIES:Orante/Feasts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:feast-2026-01-15@orante
DTSTAMP:20261019T184556Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260116
SUMMARY:⚪ St Paul the First Hermit\, Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Epiphany\nMass: Mass of the fe
 ast (Proper of Saints\, 15 Jan\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Maurus\, A
 bbot\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nEgyptian who fled the Dec
 ian persecution around 250 to a cave in the Theban desert and stayed some 
 ninety years\, dying about 341. Jerome's Life records Antony's visit to hi
 m and the raven that brought bread.\nSt Paul the First Hermit · patron of
  hermits\, weavers\, basket-makers\nDisciple of Benedict at Subiaco in the
  early 6th century\; Gregory the Great tells how he ran across the lake to
  pull the boy Placid from the water. A 9th-century legend credits him with
  founding Glanfeuil in France.\nSt Maurus · patron of the sick\, against 
 gout and rheumatism\, coppersmiths\, charcoal-burners\nLitany of Saint Mau
 rus: https://www.catholicculture.org/culture/liturgicalyear/prayers/view.c
 fm?id=1165\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.c
 om/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=01-15-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubr
 ics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.co
 m/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=01-15-2026&command=prayLaudes&version=R
 ubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nVespers: https://www.divinumoffici
 um.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=01-15-2026&command=prayVesperae&ve
 rsion=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nCompline: https://www.divin
 umofficium.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=01-15-2026&command=prayCom
 pletorium&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
CATEGORIES:Orante/Feasts
END:VEVENT
