SUMMARY:🟢 Monday (feria)
DESCRIPTION:IV class · green · Time after Epiphany\nMass: Mass of the pre
 ceding Sunday (or a votive / daily Mass for the dead)\nCommemorations: Sts
  Marius\, Martha\, Audifax & Abachum\, Martyrs\; St Canute\, King & Martyr
 \nGloria no · Credo no · Preface: Trinity\nA Persian nobleman\, his wife
 \, and two sons who came to Rome about 270 to venerate the martyrs and bur
 y the dead. Arrested under Claudius II\; Martha was drowned and the men be
 headed on the Via Cornelia.\nCanute IV\, king of Denmark from 1080\, who e
 nforced tithes and church law against resistance. Rebels killed him before
  the altar of St Alban's church at Odense on 10 July 1086\; canonized 1101
 \, Denmark's first saint.\nSt Canute · patron of Denmark\nMass propers (D
 ivinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?
 date1=01-19-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2
