SUMMARY:⚪ St Peter Nolasco\, Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Epiphany\nMass: Mass of the fe
 ast (Proper of Saints\, 28 Jan\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Agnes (sec
 ond feast)\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nMerchant from Langu
 edoc (c. 1189–1256) who founded the Order of Our Lady of Mercy at Barcel
 ona in 1218 to ransom Christians held captive by the Moors. Members vowed 
 to offer themselves in exchange if needed.\nSt Peter Nolasco · patron of 
 captives\, prisoners\, Mercedarians\nNovena to Saint Peter Nolasco: https:
 //www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/novenas/p03931.htm\nThe octave day of St A
 gnes\, kept at Rome since at least the 7th century. The ancient Acts tell 
 that eight days after her death she appeared to her parents at her tomb\, 
 surrounded by virgins and holding a lamb.\nSt Agnes (second feast) · patr
 on of young girls\, chastity\, virgins\, betrothed couples\, rape victims\
 , gardeners\nSt. Agnes Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-agnes-no
 vena\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi
 -bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=01-28-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%20
 1960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-
 bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=01-28-2026&command=prayLaudes&version=Rubrics
 %201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nVespers: https://www.divinumofficium.com
 /cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=01-28-2026&command=prayVesperae&version=
