SUMMARY:⚪ St Titus\, Bishop & Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Septuagesima\nMass: Mass of the feast (Pr
 oper of Saints\, 6 Feb\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Dorothy\, Virgin &
  Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nFast: Abstinence from 
 meat (no fast)\nGreek convert and companion of Paul\, who left him on Cret
 e to organize the churches there and addressed an epistle to him. Traditio
 n says he died in old age at Gortyna around the end of the 1st century.\nS
 t Titus · patron of Crete\nSt. Titus Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.
 com/st-titus-novena\nVirgin of Caesarea in Cappadocia beheaded about 304 u
 nder Diocletian. The legend tells that a child brought roses and apples fr
 om paradise to the lawyer Theophilus\, who had mocked her on the way to ex
 ecution.\nSt Dorothy · patron of gardeners\, florists\, brewers\, brides\
 , newlyweds\, midwives\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divin
 umofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=02-06-2026&command=prayMissa&
 version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinu
