SUMMARY:⚪ St Casimir\, Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Lent\nMass: Mass of the feast (Proper of 
 Saints\, 4 Mar\, or Common)\nAd libitum: Mass of the feria with commemorat
 ion of St Casimir\, Confessor\, or Mass of the feast with commemoration of
  the feria.\nCommemorations: Wednesday of Lent\; St Lucius I\, Pope & Mart
 yr\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Lent\nFast: Fast only (meat permitt
 ed at the principal meal)\nPrince of Poland (1458–1484)\, son of King Ca
 simir IV\, who declined the Hungarian crown offered him in 1471 and lived 
 in chastity and prayer. Died of tuberculosis at Grodno aged 25\; buried at
  Vilnius.\nSt Casimir · patron of Poland\, Lithuania\, youth\, bachelors\
 , princes\nNovena to Saint Casimir: https://www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/
 novenas/p03935.htm\nPope from 253 to 254\, banished under Gallus and soon 
 recalled\; continued Cornelius's mild policy toward Christians who had lap
 sed in persecution. Died peacefully but honored as a martyr\; buried in th
 e cemetery of Callixtus.\nSt Lucius I · patron of Copenhagen\nMass proper
 s (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa
 .pl?date1=03-04-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&l
