SUMMARY:🔴 Sts Perpetua & Felicitas\, Martyrs
DESCRIPTION:III class · red · Lent\nMass: Mass of the feast (Proper of Sa
 ints\, 6 Mar\, or Common)\nAd libitum: Mass of the feria with commemoratio
 n of Sts Perpetua & Felicitas\, Martyrs\, or Mass of the feast with commem
 oration of the feria.\nCommemorations: Friday of Lent\nGloria yes · Credo
  no · Preface: Lent\nFast: Fast and complete abstinence\nPerpetua\, a 22-
 year-old noblewoman nursing an infant\, and Felicitas\, a slave who gave b
 irth in prison\, were killed by beasts in the amphitheater of Carthage on 
 7 March 203. Perpetua's own prison diary survives.\nSts Perpetua & Felicit
 as · patron of mothers\, expectant mothers\, ranchers\, butchers\, Cartha
 ge\nNovena to Saints Perpetua and Felicity: https://www.praymorenovenas.co
 m/novena-to-saints-perpetua-and-felicity\nMass propers (Divinum Officium):
