 tion of St Gregory the Great\, Pope\, Confessor & Doctor\, or Mass of the 
 feast with commemoration of the feria.\nCommemorations: Thursday of Lent\n
 Gloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Lent\nFast: Fast only (meat permitted 
 at the principal meal)\nRoman prefect turned monk (c. 540–604)\, pope fr
 om 590\, who sent Augustine to England in 596 and wrote the Pastoral Rule\
 , Dialogues\, and Moralia on Job. The Roman chant and liturgy bear his nam
 e.\nSt Gregory the Great · patron of musicians\, singers\, students\, tea
 chers\, popes\, masons\, England\, against plague\nSt. Gregory the Great N
 ovena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-gregory-the-great-novena\nMass p
