DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260415
SUMMARY:🔴 St Justin\, Martyr
DESCRIPTION:III class · red · Paschaltide\nMass: Mass of the feast (Prope
 r of Saints\, 14 Apr\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Tiburtius\, Valeria
 n & Maximus\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Easter\nPhilosop
 her from Flavia Neapolis in Samaria (c. 100–165) who taught Christianity
  at Rome in a philosopher's cloak. His two Apologies describe 2nd-century 
 baptism and Eucharist\; beheaded with six companions under Marcus Aurelius
 .\nSt Justin · patron of philosophers\, apologists\, lecturers\, orators\
 nSt. Justin Martyr Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-justin-marty
 r-novena\nValerian\, husband of Cecilia\, his brother Tiburtius\, and Maxi
 mus\, the officer converted at their execution\, beheaded at Rome\, tradit
 ionally about 230. Buried in the cemetery of Praetextatus on the Via Appia
 .\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bi
 n/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=04-14-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%20196
 0%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin
