DESCRIPTION:II class · red · Paschaltide\nMass: Mass of the feast (Proper
  of Saints\, 11 May\, or Common)\nCommemorations: none\nGloria yes · Cred
 o yes · Preface: Apostles\nMarks: Rogation\nRogation Monday (Minor Litani
 es): Procession with the Litany of the Saints and Mass of Rogations (viole
 t) where held\; otherwise commemoration.\nPhilip of Bethsaida\, who brough
 t Nathanael to Jesus\, and James son of Alphaeus\, first bishop of Jerusal
 em\, thrown from the Temple and clubbed in 62. The joint feast dates from 
 the dedication of their basilica at Rome about 570.\nSts Philip & James ·
  patron of St Philip: hatters\, pastry-chefs\, Luxembourg\; St James: full
 ers\, pharmacists\, the dying\nSaints Philip and James Novena: https://www
 .praymorenovenas.com/saints-philip-and-james-novena\nMass propers (Divinum
