SUMMARY:🔴 Sts Nereus\, Achilleus\, Domitilla & Pancras\, Martyrs
DESCRIPTION:III class · red · Paschaltide\nMass: Mass of the feast (Prope
 r of Saints\, 12 May\, or Common)\nCommemorations: none\nGloria yes · Cre
 do no · Preface: Easter\nMarks: Rogation\nRogation Tuesday (Minor Litanie
 s): Procession with the Litany of the Saints and Mass of Rogations (violet
 ) where held\; otherwise commemoration.\nNereus and Achilleus\, soldiers w
 ho refused to serve\, were beheaded in the late 1st century and buried in 
 the catacomb of Domitilla. Domitilla\, Domitian's niece\, was exiled in 95
 \; Pancras\, aged 14\, was beheaded at Rome in 304.\nSts Nereus · patron 
 of St Pancras: children\, oaths\, against headaches\, cramps\, false witne
 ss\nSt. Pancras Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-pancras-novena\
