SUMMARY:⚪ St Peter Celestine\, Pope & Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Paschaltide\nMass: Mass of the feast (Pro
 per of Saints\, 19 May\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Pudentiana\, Virgi
 n\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Easter\nHermit of the Maiella (c. 12
 15–1296) and founder of the Celestine monks\, elected pope as Celestine 
 V in July 1294 after a two-year vacancy. Resigned after five months\; Boni
 face VIII confined him at Fumone\, where he died.\nSt Peter Celestine · p
 atron of bookbinders\, hermits\, L'Aquila\, Molise\nPope St. Celestine V N
 ovena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/pope-st-celestine-v-novena\nRoman v
 irgin of the 2nd century\, by tradition daughter of the senator Pudens who
  hosted Peter. Her title church on the Viminal is among the oldest in Rome
 \; scholars suspect the name arose from 'ecclesia Pudentiana'\, the church
  of Pudens.\nSt Pudentiana · patron of the Philippines\nMass propers (Div
 inum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?da
 te1=05-19-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=E
 nglish\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?
