  yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nAnglo-Saxon princess born in Hungary 
 (c. 1045–1093)\, who married Malcolm III of Scotland about 1070. Brought
  Scottish usage into line with Rome\, founded Dunfermline\, and died four 
 days after her husband fell at Alnwick.\nSt Margaret · patron of Scotland
 \, widows\, large families\, learning\, queens\, loss of children\nSt. Mar
 garet of Scotland Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-margaret-of-s
 cotland\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/
