SUMMARY:⚪ St Ephrem the Syrian\, Deacon\, Confessor & Doctor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 18 Jun\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Mark & M
 arcellian\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Common\nSyriac de
 acon (c. 306-373) of Nisibis and later Edessa who wrote theology as hymns 
 and verse homilies\, earning the title Harp of the Holy Spirit. Benedict X
 V named him a Doctor in 1920.\nSt Ephrem the Syrian · patron of spiritual
  directors\, spiritual leaders\nSt. Ephrem the Syrian Novena: https://www.
 praymorenovenas.com/st-ephrem-the-syrian-novena\nTwin brothers of Rome\, d
 eacons by tradition\, martyred under Diocletian about 286 after St Sebasti
 an steadied their resolve. They were buried on the Via Ardeatina\, where t
 heir tomb was found in 1902.\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www
 .divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=06-18-2026&command=pray
 Missa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.
