 east (Proper of Saints\, 19 Jun\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Gervase 
 & Protase\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nFast: Abst
 inence from meat (no fast)\nFlorentine (1270-1341)\, niece of a founding S
 ervite\, who established the Servite Third Order sisters known as the Mant
 ellate. Unable to swallow the Host when dying\, she is said to have receiv
 ed it miraculously through her breast.\nSt Juliana Falconieri · patron of
  the chronically ill\, bodily ills\nSt. Juliana Falconieri Novena: https:/
 /www.praymorenovenas.com/st-juliana-falconieri-novena\nThe first martyrs o
 f Milan\, of unknown date\, whose bodies St Ambrose discovered in 386 and 
 translated to his new basilica. The find\, attended by reported healings\,
  strengthened Ambrose against the Arian court.\nSts Gervase & Protase · p
 atron of Milan\, haymakers\, discovery of thieves\nMass propers (Divinum O
 fficium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=06
