SUMMARY:🔴 Commemoration of St Paul\, Apostle
DESCRIPTION:III class · red · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the fea
 st (Proper of Saints\, 30 Jun\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Peter\, Apo
 stle\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Apostles\nThe day after the join
 t feast\, Rome honors Paul alone: apostle to the Gentiles\, author of thir
 teen letters\, beheaded at Aquae Salviae about 67 and buried where St Paul
  Outside the Walls now stands.\nCommemoration of St Paul · patron of miss
 ionaries\, evangelists\, writers\, theologians\, Malta\, Rome\nNovena to S
 aints Peter and Paul: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/novena-to-saints-pet
 er-and-paul\nCommemoration of Peter within the Mass of St Paul on June 30\
 , keeping the two apostles paired. Fisherman of Bethsaida\, first bishop o
 f Rome\, crucified head downward under Nero about 64 and buried on the Vat
 ican hill.\nSt Peter · patron of popes\, fishermen\, locksmiths\, net-mak
 ers\, the universal Church\nLitany of St. Peter\, Prince of the Apostles: 
 https://www.catholicculture.org/culture/liturgicalyear/prayers/view.cfm?id
 =1141\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cg
