 avia in 863\, who devised the Glagolitic alphabet and translated the litur
 gy and Scriptures into Slavonic. Cyril died in Rome in 869\; Methodius\, a
 rchbishop of Pannonia\, in 885.\nSts Cyril & Methodius · patron of Europe
  (co-patrons)\, Slavic peoples\, ecumenism\, unity of East and West\nMass 
 propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/
 Pmissa.pl?date1=07-07-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%20
