 sa & her seven sons\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\n
 Soldier and gambler from the Abruzzi (1550-1614) who\, after conversion\, 
 founded in Rome in 1582 the Ministers of the Sick\, who nursed plague vict
 ims and the wounded on battlefields under a red cross on their habit.\nSt 
 Camillus de Lellis · patron of the sick\, hospitals\, nurses\, physicians
 \, against gambling\nSt. Camillus de Lellis Novena: https://www.praymoreno
 venas.com/st-camillus-de-lellis-novena\nWidow of the martyr Getulius\, put
  to death at Tivoli under Hadrian around 120 for refusing to sacrifice at 
 his new villa. She was drowned in the Anio and her seven sons killed the n
 ext day.\nPrayer for the Feast of St. Symphorosa and Her Seven Sons: https
 ://www.catholicculture.org/culture/liturgicalyear/prayers/view.cfm?id=1453
 \nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin
