 t (Proper of Saints\, 25 Jul\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Christopher\
 , Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Apostles\nSon of Zebedee and
  brother of John\, among the three closest to Jesus\, beheaded by Herod Ag
 rippa I in 44\, the first apostle to die (Acts 12). His tomb at Compostela
  became the chief pilgrimage of medieval Europe.\nSt James · patron of Sp
 ain\, pilgrims\, labourers\, veterinarians\, equestrians\, arthritis suffe
 rers\nSt. James the Greater Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-jam
 es-the-greater-novena\nMartyr in Lycia\, Asia Minor\, about 250 under Deci
 us. The medieval legend of a giant who carried the Christ Child across a r
 iver grew from his name\, Christ-bearer\; he is one of the Fourteen Holy H
 elpers.\nSt Christopher · patron of travellers\, motorists\, sailors\, ag
 ainst storms\, toothache\, sudden death\nSt. Christopher Novena: https://w
 ww.praymorenovenas.com/st-christopher-novena\nMass propers (Divinum Offici
