DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 29 Jul\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Felix\, 
 Simplicius\, Faustinus & Beatrice\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Pre
 face: Common\nSister of Mary and Lazarus at Bethany\, who served Jesus at 
 table and professed him the Christ before Lazarus was raised (John 11). Pr
 ovencal legend brought her to Tarascon\, where her tomb is venerated.\nSt 
 Martha · patron of cooks\, housekeepers\, servants\, innkeepers\, waiters
 \, dietitians\nSt. Martha Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-marth
 a-novena\nSimplicius and Faustinus\, brothers\, were drowned in the Tiber 
 about 303 under Diocletian\; their sister Beatrice was strangled after bur
 ying them at Generosa on the Via Portuensis. Felix is the antipope Felix I
 I\, long mistaken for a martyr.\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://
 www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=07-29-2026&command=p
 rayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://w
