 ast (Proper of Saints\, 6 Aug\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Sixtus II\
 , Pope\, Felicissimus & Agapitus\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Pre
 face: Nativity\nPope Sixtus II was seized while preaching in the cemetery 
 of Callixtus and beheaded on 6 August 258 under Valerian\, with four deaco
 ns. The deacons Felicissimus and Agapitus died the same day and were burie
 d in the cemetery of Praetextatus.\nPrayer for the Feast of St. Sixtus and
  Companions: https://catholicculture.org/culture/liturgicalyear/prayers/vi
 ew.cfm?id=1460\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumoffici
