 , Largus & Smaragdus\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\
 nParish priest of Ars near Lyon (1786-1859)\, a struggling seminarian who 
 became a confessor sought by pilgrims from across France\, spending up to 
 sixteen hours a day in the confessional. Canonized in 1925.\nSt John Mary 
 Vianney · patron of parish priests\, confessors\nSt. John Vianney Novena:
  https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st-john-vianney-novena\nRoman martyrs\, C
 yriacus a deacon\, executed about 305 under Diocletian and Maximian. First
  buried on the Via Ostiensis\, their remains were moved by Pope Marcellus 
 to the Via Salaria\; Cyriacus is a Fourteen Holy Helper.\nSts Cyriacus · 
 patron of St Cyriacus: eye disease\, demonic possession\, temptation at de
 ath\; Fourteen Holy Helpers\nPrayer for the Feast of St. Cyriacus\, Largus
