DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 28 Aug\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Hermes\, 
 Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Common\nFast: Abstinence from 
 meat (no fast)\nBorn at Thagaste in North Africa in 354\, converted at Mil
 an in 386\, bishop of Hippo from 395 until his death in 430 during the Van
 dal siege. His Confessions and City of God shaped all later Western theolo
 gy.\nSt Augustine · patron of theologians\, printers\, brewers\, sore eye
 s\, Augustinians\nSt. Augustine Novena: https://www.praymorenovenas.com/st
 -augustine-novena\nRoman martyr of the early 2nd or 3rd century\, buried i
 n the cemetery of Basilla on the Via Salaria Vetus. His feast appears in t
 he Depositio Martyrum of 354\; legend made him a prefect of Rome.\nMass pr
 opers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pm
 issa.pl?date1=08-28-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%2019
