DESCRIPTION:III class · red · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the fea
 st (Proper of Saints\, 29 Aug\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Sabina\, Ma
 rtyr\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nCommemorates John's execu
 tion by Herod Antipas at Salome's request (Mark 6). The date comes from th
 e dedication of a church at Sebaste in Samaria\, his traditional tomb\; Ro
 me kept it by the 5th century.\nBeheading of St John the Baptist · patron
  of baptism\, converts\, tailors\, monastic life\, Jordan\, Quebec\, Puert
 o Rico\nLitany to St. John the Baptist: https://www.ewtn.com/catholicism/d
 evotions/litany-to-st-john-the-baptist-258\nRoman matron martyred under Ha
 drian about 126\, according to her acts\, after conversion by her slave Se
 rapia. The 5th-century basilica of Santa Sabina on the Aventine stands on 
 the site identified as her house.\nSt Sabina · patron of housewives\nMass
  propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa
