 Preface: Common\nHermit of the 7th or 8th century near Nimes in Provence\,
  said to have been wounded by a king's arrow aimed at the hind that fed hi
 m. The abbey of Saint-Gilles grew over his tomb\; a Fourteen Holy Helper.\
 nSt Giles · patron of beggars\, the disabled\, lepers\, blacksmiths\, bre
 astfeeding\, Edinburgh\; Fourteen Holy Helpers\nCollect for the Feast of S
 aint Giles: https://www.catholic.org/prayers/prayer.php?p=3251\nTwelve Afr
 ican martyrs who died under Valerian about 258\, whose relics Duke Arechis
  II gathered at Benevento in 760. The legend that they were sons of St Bon
 iface and St Thecla of Hadrumetum grew from that translation.\nMass proper
 s (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa
