 st (Proper of Saints\, 16 Sep\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Euphemia\,
  Lucy & Geminian\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nCor
 nelius was pope 251 to 253 and died in exile at Civitavecchia\; Cyprian\, 
 bishop of Carthage\, was beheaded in 258 under Valerian. Allies by letter\
 , both resisted the rigorists over readmitting lapsed Christians.\nSts Cor
 nelius · patron of St Cornelius: cattle\, against earache\, fever\, epile
 psy\; St Cyprian: North Africa\, Algeria\nSt. Cyprian Novena: https://www.
 praymorenovenas.com/st-cyprian-novena\nEuphemia was a virgin martyred at C
 halcedon about 303\; her basilica there housed the council of 451. Lucy an
 d Geminian are recorded as martyrs at Rome of uncertain date\, joined to h
 er on this day.\nSts Euphemia · patron of St Euphemia: Chalcedon\, Rovinj
 \nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin
