 eceding Sunday (or a votive / daily Mass for the dead)\nCommemorations: St
  Placid & Companions\, Martyrs\nGloria no · Credo no · Preface: Common\n
 Placid was a boy disciple of St Benedict at Subiaco in the 6th century. A 
 medieval forgery made him a martyr at Messina\, Sicily\, with 30 companion
 s killed by raiders about 541\; the cult outlived the discredited story.\n
 St Placid & Companions · patron of St Placid: novices\, against chills an
