 east (Proper of Saints\, 8 Oct\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Sergius\,
  Bacchus\, Marcellus & Apuleius\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Prefa
 ce: Common\nSwedish noblewoman (about 1303-1373) and mother of eight who a
 fter her husband's death founded the Brigittine order at Vadstena\; lived 
 in Rome from 1349 urging the popes to return from Avignon. Her Revelations
  were widely read.\nSt Bridget · patron of Sweden\, Europe\, widows\, sch
 olars\nNovena to St. Bridget of Sweden: https://www.catholicdoors.com/pray
 ers/novenas/p03682.htm\nSergius and Bacchus were Roman officers martyred i
 n Syria about 303\; Sergius's tomb at Resafa became a major pilgrimage shr
 ine. Marcellus and Apuleius are Roman martyrs of uncertain date buried nea
 r the city.\nSts Sergius · patron of Sts Sergius & Bacchus: soldiers\, Sy
 ria\, Arab Christians\nNovena to Saint Sergius and Saint Bacchus: https://
