SUMMARY:🟢 Wednesday (feria)
DESCRIPTION:IV class · green · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the pr
 eceding Sunday (or a votive / daily Mass for the dead)\nCommemorations: St
  Hilarion\, Abbot\; Sts Ursula & Companions\, Virgins & Martyrs\nGloria no
  · Credo no · Preface: Common\nBorn near Gaza about 291\, disciple of An
 thony in Egypt\; introduced monasticism to Palestine about 306\, then fled
  his fame to Sicily\, Dalmatia and Cyprus\, where he died in 371. His Life
  was written by Jerome.\nSt Hilarion · patron of hermits\, Cyprus\nA Brit
 ish princess and her virgin companions\, said to have been killed by Huns 
 at Cologne while returning from Rome\, perhaps in the 4th or 5th century. 
 A 4th-century inscription attests virgin martyrs at Cologne\; the figure 1
 1\,000 is medieval.\nSts Ursula & Companions · patron of St Ursula: stude
 nts\, schoolgirls\, teachers\, Cologne\, Ursulines\, a holy death\nNovena 
 to Saint Ursula and Companions: https://www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/nove
 nas/p03891.htm\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumoffici
 um.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=10-21-2026&command=prayMissa&version=
