SUMMARY:⚪ St Charles Borromeo\, Bishop & Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 4 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Vitalis &
  Agricola\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nCardinal-n
 ephew of Pius IV at 22 (1538-1584)\, archbishop of Milan from 1564\; helpe
 d bring the Council of Trent to a close and enforced its reforms through s
 eminaries\, synods and visitations. Nursed Milan through the plague of 157
 6.\nSt Charles Borromeo · patron of bishops\, catechists\, seminarians\, 
 spiritual directors\, against ulcers and intestinal disorders\nLitany of S
 aint Charles Borromeo: https://www.catholicculture.org/culture/liturgicaly
 ear/prayers/view.cfm?id=1169\nMartyrs at Bologna under Diocletian about 30
 4\; Vitalis\, the slave of Agricola\, died first under torture and Agricol
 a was crucified. Ambrose discovered their bodies in 393 and spread the cul
 t.\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-b
 in/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=11-04-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%2019
 60%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bi
