SUMMARY:⚪ Dedication of the Archbasilica of the Most Holy Saviour (Latera
 n) (II)
DESCRIPTION:II class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the fe
 ast (Proper of Saints\, 9 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Theodore\, 
 Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nCommemorates the dedica
 tion by Pope Sylvester\, about 324\, of the basilica Constantine built on 
 the Lateran estate\, the cathedral of Rome and mother and head of all chur
 ches. First dedicated to the Savior\, later also to the two Johns.\nSoldie
 r called Tyro\, the recruit\, burned at Amasea in Pontus about 306 after s
 etting fire to a temple of Cybele. One of the most honored Eastern martyrs
 \; the church of San Teodoro stands below the Palatine in Rome.\nSt Theodo
 re · patron of soldiers\, recruits\, Venice\, Brindisi\, against storms\n
 Mass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/m
 issa/Pmissa.pl?date1=11-09-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%2
 0-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/ho
