SUMMARY:⚪ St Andrew Avellino\, Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 10 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: Sts Tryphon\
 , Respicius & Nympha\, Martyrs\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\
 nNeapolitan lawyer (1521-1608) who became a Theatine priest after telling 
 a lie in court\; spent decades reforming convents and preaching in Naples 
 and Lombardy. Collapsed from a stroke while beginning Mass. Canonized 1712
 .\nSt Andrew Avellino · patron of Naples\, Sicily\, against sudden death\
 , apoplexy and stroke\nNovena to Saint Andrew Avellino: https://www.cathol
 icdoors.com/prayers/novenas/p04059.htm\nTryphon\, a gooseherd of Phrygia\,
  was martyred at Nicaea about 250 with Respicius\; Nympha was a virgin of 
 Palermo of uncertain date. Their relics were brought together at Rome\, he
 nce the common feast.\nSts Tryphon · patron of St Tryphon: gardeners\, vi
 ne-growers\, against pests and rodents\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): h
 ttps://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=11-10-2026&co
 mmand=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: ht
