DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:⚪ St Martin\, Bishop & Confessor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 11 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Mennas\, 
 Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nSoldier from Pannonia (
 about 316-397) who divided his cloak with a beggar at Amiens\; founded Lig
 ugé\, the first monastery in Gaul\, and was bishop of Tours from 371. Amo
 ng the first non-martyrs given a public cult.\nSt Martin · patron of sold
 iers\, France\, beggars\, tailors\, innkeepers\, vintners\, horses\, geese
 \nNovena to Saint Martin of Tours: https://www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/n
 ovenas/p03906.htm\nEgyptian soldier martyred under Diocletian about 300\; 
 his shrine at Abu Mina west of Alexandria was a major pilgrimage center of
  the 5th and 6th centuries\, whose oil flasks have been found across the M
 editerranean.\nSt Mennas · patron of merchants\, travellers\, caravans\, 
 falsely accused\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumoffic
 ium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=11-11-2026&command=prayMissa&version
 =Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumoffici
 um.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-11-2026&command=prayLaudes&vers
 ion=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nVespers: https://www.divinumo
 fficium.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-11-2026&command=prayVesper
 ae&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nCompline: https://www.
 divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-11-2026&command=pr
 ayCompletorium&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English
