SUMMARY:⚪ St Elizabeth of Hungary\, Widow
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 19 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Pontianus
 \, Pope & Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nDaughter of K
 ing Andrew II (1207-1231)\, married at 14 to Landgrave Louis of Thuringia\
 ; widowed at 20\, she became a Franciscan tertiary and spent her last year
 s nursing the poor in a hospital she built at Marburg. Canonized 1235.\nSt
  Elizabeth of Hungary · patron of bakers\, beggars\, brides\, widows\, ho
 spitals\, nurses\, charities\, Third Order Franciscans\nLitany in Honour o
 f Saint Elizabeth of Hungary: https://www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/litani
 es/p03547.htm\nPope 230 to 235\, deported with Hippolytus to the mines of 
 Sardinia by Maximinus Thrax\; resigned the papacy\, the first pope known t
 o do so\, and died there. His body was brought back to the cemetery of Cal
 listus.\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/
 cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=11-19-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics
 %201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/c
 gi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-19-2026&command=prayLaudes&version=Rubr
