SUMMARY:🔴 St Clement I\, Pope & Martyr
DESCRIPTION:III class · red · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the fea
 st (Proper of Saints\, 23 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Felicitas\,
  Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo no · Preface: Common\nThird successor of Pet
 er\, pope about 88 to 97\; his letter to the Corinthians is the earliest C
 hristian writing outside the New Testament. Later legend has him exiled to
  the Crimea and drowned with an anchor.\nSt Clement I · patron of mariner
 s\, sailors\, stonecutters\, marble workers\, blacksmiths\nNovena to Saint
  Clement of Rome: https://www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/novenas/p03895.htm
 \nRoman widow martyred about 165 under Marcus Aurelius after watching her 
 seven sons die\; buried in the cemetery of Maximus on the Via Salaria. The
  sons are honored July 10\; the story's historicity is debated.\nSt Felici
 tas · patron of mothers\, parents who have lost children\, against steril
 ity\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-
 bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=11-23-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201
 960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-b
 in/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-23-2026&command=prayLaudes&version=Rubrics%
