SUMMARY:⚪ St John of the Cross\, Confessor & Doctor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the f
 east (Proper of Saints\, 24 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: St Chrysogon
 us\, Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Common\nCastilian Carmeli
 te (1542-1591) who joined Teresa's reform in 1568\; imprisoned nine months
  at Toledo by the unreformed friars\, where he began the Spiritual Canticl
 e. His Ascent\, Dark Night and Living Flame earned him the title Doctor in
  1926.\nSt John of the Cross · patron of contemplatives\, mystics\, Spani
 sh poets\nLitany in Honour of Saint John of the Cross: https://www.catholi
 cdoors.com/prayers/litanies/p03556.htm\nMartyr beheaded at Aquileia about 
 304 under Diocletian\; his cult was carried to Rome\, where the title chur
 ch of San Crisogono in Trastevere bears his name and he is named in the Ro
 man Canon.\nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.c
 om/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl?date1=11-24-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubr
 ics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nLauds: https://www.divinumofficium.co
 m/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-24-2026&command=prayLaudes&version=R
 ubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nVespers: https://www.divinumoffici
 um.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-24-2026&command=prayVesperae&ve
 rsion=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English\nCompline: https://www.divin
 umofficium.com/cgi-bin/horas/Pofficium.pl?date1=11-24-2026&command=prayCom
 pletorium&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lang2=English
