DESCRIPTION:III class · red · Time after Pentecost\nMass: Mass of the fea
 st (Proper of Saints\, 25 Nov\, or Common)\nCommemorations: none\nGloria y
 es · Credo no · Preface: Common\nVirgin of Alexandria said to have confo
 unded 50 philosophers before the emperor Maxentius\, been bound to a spike
 d wheel that broke\, and been beheaded about 305. No early evidence surviv
 es\; her shrine at Mount Sinai dates from the 9th century.\nSt Catherine 
 · patron of philosophers\, students\, scholars\, lawyers\, librarians\, u
 nmarried girls\, wheelwrights\, millers\, nurses\nNovena to Saint Catherin
 e of Alexandria: https://www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/novenas/p03702.htm\
 nMass propers (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/
