SUMMARY:⚪ St Peter Chrysologus\, Bishop\, Confessor & Doctor
DESCRIPTION:III class · white · Advent\nMass: Mass of the feast (Proper o
 f Saints\, 4 Dec\, or Common)\nAd libitum: Mass of the feria with commemor
 ation of St Peter Chrysologus\, Bishop\, Confessor & Doctor\, or Mass of t
 he feast with commemoration of the feria.\nCommemorations: Friday of Adven
 t\; St Barbara\, Virgin & Martyr\nGloria yes · Credo yes · Preface: Comm
 on\nFast: Abstinence from meat (no fast)\nBishop of Ravenna\, then the imp
 erial capital\, from about 433 to 450\; surnamed golden-worded for his sho
 rt\, plain sermons\, some 180 of which survive. Declared Doctor in 1729.\n
 St Peter Chrysologus · patron of Imola\, Ravenna\, against fever and rabi
 es\nNovena to Saint Peter Chrysologus: https://www.catholicdoors.com/praye
 rs/novenas/p03872.htm\nVirgin said to have been shut in a tower by her pag
 an father\, who beheaded her himself and was struck dead by lightning\, at
  Nicomedia in the 3rd century. No early evidence\; the cult spread from th
 e 7th century.\nSt Barbara · patron of artillerymen\, miners\, firefighte
 rs\, architects\, against lightning\, sudden death\nNovena to Saint Barbar
 a: https://www.catholicdoors.com/prayers/novenas/p03846.htm\nMass propers 
 (Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.p
 l?date1=12-04-2026&command=prayMissa&version=Rubrics%201960%20-%201960&lan
