 ancellor of Henry II (1118-1170)\, then archbishop from 1162\; defended cl
 erical jurisdiction against the king\, spent six years in French exile\, a
 nd was killed by four knights in his cathedral on December 29. Canonized 1
 173.\nSt Thomas of Canterbury · patron of secular clergy\, Exeter College
  Oxford\, Portsmouth\nPrayer for St. Thomas a Becket: https://www.catholic
 culture.org/culture/liturgicalyear/prayers/view.cfm?id=961\nMass propers (
 Divinum Officium): https://www.divinumofficium.com/cgi-bin/missa/Pmissa.pl
